  "description": "Flat 362 Lauderdale Tower has already been extensively refurbished and the kitchen and living room layout remodelled in 2006, Listed Building Consent was sought at the time by the then owners, and approval was granted for the work (your reference: 06/00656/LBC).\n\nOur current proposal includes stripping out the existing open plan kitchen and associated utility room space dating from the 2006 refurbishment, and refitting them. We will also strip out and refit the existing bathroom and separate shower/WC, both of which also date from the 2006 refurbishment (Please note: Listed Building Consent is not required for the work to the bathroom or separate shower/WC). In addition, we will be slightly reconfiguring the layouts of the three bedrooms by removing non-structural walls separating Bedrooms 1 and 2 and Bedroom 3 and the living room; these walls will be rebuilt in new studwork to slightly adjust the footprints of the three bedrooms. We will also be replacing all internal doors with new full-height doors and installing a shallow false ceiling throughout the flat to allow for the installation of inset spotlighting.\n",
